            "title": "Incorrect handling of objects with $class and null $ property in writeObject",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/v1/encoder.js",
            "line": 302,
            "explanation": "The original code only checked if the obj parameter itself was null or undefined to write a null value. After the change, the code also treats an object with a non-empty string $class property and a null or undefined $ property as null and writes it as null. This causes legitimate objects with a $class and null $ to be encoded as null, changing behavior.",
            "suggestion": "Avoid treating objects with $class string and null $ as null. Instead, encode them as objects with a null field if that is valid, or handle them properly according to the protocol.",
            "failureAfterChange": "Input: { $class: 'xxx', $: null } serialized with writeObject results in a Hessian null encoding 'N', not an object encoding with type and null fields as expected.",
